comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-29T04:41:47.927Z","harness:claude-code","Sibling class measured 2026-07-29 in the same record this item censuses: the author field of the same 41,021 entries holds 477 distinct spellings with no enumeration, no contract entry and no gate, and four of its six most frequent values are two harnesses written two ways. It is the same ungoverned-value-domain shape as the 71 op literals, one layer harder for the same reason - the stream is append-only, so neither vocabulary can be fixed by migration and both need read-time canonicalization against declared data. Owner for the author half is pm-3yxwv5; keep the two separate because the op vocabulary is written only by the product while the author vocabulary is also written by callers through --author and PM_AUTHOR."
  "2026-08-01T09:52:05.174Z","harness:claude-code","Live op census, 2026-08-01, over all 2,258 history streams and 42,771 entries. 37 distinct op literals are actually written: update 10,931, comment_add 8,010, files_add 6,592, tests_add 3,086, claim 2,745, release 2,281, create 2,215, close 2,202, docs_add 1,431, test_run_track 913, note_add 725, learning_add 636, update_audit 309, update_ownership_bypass 120, append 115, plan_complete_step 85, plan_add_step 71, plan_update_step 44, history_repair 42, history_compact_baseline 41, history_compact 41, history_redact 23, plan_create_metadata 19, history:author-acknowledge 9, plan_create_initial_step 12, plan_append_discovery 12, delete 12, plan_append_validation 9, plan_append_decision 7, plan_approve 6, plan_link_step 4, comment_edit 4, comment_delete 3, plan_unlink_step 1, plan_reorder_step 1, note_delete 1. The naming-convention finding is confirmed and is now a single outlier: history:author-acknowledge is the one colon-namespaced literal in the entire immutable record; every other op is snake_case, and the plan_* family is the one that uses a namespace prefix without a separator. That makes the canonicalization tractable -- one recorded spelling has to move, not a class of them. The gap between 37 written and ~71 declared is also the measurement pm-pww8ax needs: half the declared vocabulary has never been exercised on a real workspace."
  "2026-09-11T10:04:52.063Z","harness:codex","TDD evidence: writer regression fails on baseline because init:type-preset is sealed unchanged. The new public operation contract separates item events, singleton events, parameterized families, explicit legacy aliases, and package-qualified custom operations. Raw historical reads remain byte-preserving. Original census also included JSON Patch verbs, onWrite hook labels, and telemetry spans; those are separate contracts and must not be renamed as history operations."
  "2026-09-11T10:10:19.682Z","harness:codex","Compatibility finding: public workspace-history APIs and package consumers already provide custom operation identities, including unqualified snake_case names. Rejecting every name outside the native inventory would break supported SDK customization. New record construction therefore validates the declared compatibility grammar and canonicalizes known aliases; a separate exhaustive source test rejects undeclared native literals. This preserves universal SDK authoring while preventing native vocabulary drift."
  "2026-09-11T10:19:10.877Z","harness:codex","Integration evidence: 47 focused tests pass across native operation grammar/runtime projections, source inventory, deleted-item recovery, schema migration retries, and author attribution. Existing author acknowledgment identities remain stable. Core shell-safe command rendering is shared with SDK exports to avoid an inverted dependency. Full exact coverage is running; no acceptance thresholds or exclusions changed."
  "2026-09-11T10:22:01.812Z","harness:codex","Current external inventory: no open GitHub PRs or issues at inspection; all three security-alert inventories were empty, and pnpm audit reports zero vulnerabilities. pm-changelog latest is 2026.9.11. Current Sentry/telemetry required-mode threshold gate passed with zero critical/high issues in the 14-day window; physical queue delivery is verified separately at closeout."
  "2026-09-11T10:23:29.673Z","harness:codex","Complete graph inspection covered all 2736 recorded items and 13642 directed edges across every lifecycle state. No missing references, ordering cycles, ordering contradictions, isolated nodes, or degree-one nodes were reported; all non-outcome nodes reached declared outcomes. Seven historical nodes retain informational hierarchy-cardinality/direction findings. The delivery adds evidence-backed verifies links to completed pm-bbk8we, rather than synthetic edges to increase depth. Only pm-0elqjj and pm-nb4zwz are in progress."
  "2026-09-11T10:32:41.299Z","harness:codex","Dynamic-family TDD found a catalogue omission: the schema migration request union includes remap-status, whose immutable writer identity is schema_remap_status. A type-exhaustive Record over that public union failed before adding this identity and its compensation family. The contract snapshot now declares the actual writer vocabulary; no historical records were rewritten."
  "2026-09-11T10:35:03.723Z","harness:codex","Security and packaging verification: all GitHub Dependabot/code-scanning/secret-scanning open inventories are empty; local Trivy HIGH/CRITICAL vulnerability, secret and misconfiguration scan completed with zero findings; tracked-file credential scan and all tracked ShellCheck scripts passed. Typecheck passed all four projects. Packed npm/npx/Bun/bunx smoke passed with six package workflows and a compiled public SDK consumer."
  "2026-09-11T10:53:02.557Z","harness:codex","Implementation verification: all 8713 tests across 670 files passed. Exact coverage: 64236/64236 statements, 48920/48920 branches, 13345/13345 functions, 61538/61538 lines. All four TypeScript projects passed. Both linked operation tests passed in the final recorded run. Default-budget history contracts include vocabulary version 1. Native literal validation and typed migration-family checks govern writers while the public SDK retains well-formed custom identities. Final static and hosted review gates remain required before merge."
  "2026-09-11T11:01:37.569Z","harness:codex","Final static verification passed ESLint, zero-duplicate checks, generated contracts, repository static/documentation assurance, package boundaries, grammar/token/refusal contracts, all tracker-context assertions, SDK surface and isolated import/transport cost budgets. Graph composition found a new prose-to-edge gap between the two jointly delivered history items; added the truthful related edge, retaining their existing typed causal and verification lineage. Complete live validation found zero history drift or identity discontinuities across 2736 items; 170 pre-existing historical outcome-field gaps remain explicitly unfilled."
  "2026-09-11T11:03:26.332Z","harness:codex","Final local delivery gates passed: the static pipeline through import/transport budgets plus corrected graph-composition and record-integrity assertions are green without threshold changes. The graph correction preserves a truthful joint-delivery association and refines an existing permanent-identity association to verifies using the new wrong-subject regression. Final temporary-project acceptance and packed npm/npx/Bun/bunx SDK-consumer smoke passed; generated changelog consistency passed. Hosted review/checks and exact merged-main proof remain separate."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-11T10:29:42.526Z","harness:codex","Operation contracts must distinguish native event identities from custom SDK names, workspace retry suffixes, JSON Patch verbs, hooks and spans. A literal source census is complemented by type-exhaustive dynamic-family checks; schema remap-status produces schema_remap_status, not schema_rename_status."
